 "text": "9/29/26, 10:19 AM\nThe disconnections that have been documented are then observed, for example in the following transactions:\n\ne Display Installation\n\ne Change Installation\ne Display Device\n\ne Change Device\nThey are also observed during the following:\n\ne Meter reading\ne Billing\ne Extrapolation\n\ne Device replacement\n\nYou can disconnect disconnection objects in several disconnection documents simultaneously. The reconnection is not actually\nexecuted until the last reconnection request is received.\n\nActivities\n\nThe disconnection is usually entered using the Change Disconnection Document transaction. However, you can also define it as a\nworkflow step.\n\nConfirmation of the optional service order generated\n\ne takes place directly in Service Management\ne Can be done directly in disconnection entry\n\ne Can be controlled by making the corresponding settings in Customizing.\n\nIn Customizing under Utilities Industry . Customer Service \u2014 Process Execution = Disconnection/ Reconnection \u2014 Define\nProcessing Variants for Disconnection Documents, you can specify that the service orders or service notifications are to be closed.\n\nIn the individual confirmation status, you can define whether service orders are to be set to technically closed or not performed.\nService notifications are always closed if this has been defined in Customizing.\n\nDisconnection Document\n\nDefinition\n\nThe disconnection document is the processing unit for the agent. A disconnection document is generated for each disconnection.\nIt is used to log the process and enables you to directly reach all the entities involved.\n",
